# Security Rules

## Core Principles
* Always prefer the most secure solution when creating new code
* If there are security concerns, note them in the chat with specific risks
* Keep responses concise unless security implications require detailed explanation

## Input Validation & Sanitization
* Always validate and sanitize user inputs before processing
* Use parameterized queries for database operations
* Implement proper file upload validation and restrictions

## Data Protection
* Never store sensitive data in plain text
* Implement proper error handling without exposing internals

## Development Process
* Confirm with developer for large refactors or security-sensitive changes
* Avoid changing existing code without confirmation
* Suggest security testing for new features
* Flag areas needing security expert review
